{
  "_comment": "Historical baseline transcribed from START's Tracking Cartels infographic series (June 2020). This is a point-in-time research product, NOT current control of territory. State classes were read from the printed choropleth legend; cities/ports/flows were interpreted from map symbol positions and are approximate. State classes were sampled from the printed choropleth at each state's centroid; Chihuahua and Guanajuato were read visually (centroid covered by a label/arrow).",
  "provider": "START (National Consortium for the Study of Terrorism and Responses to Terrorism), University of Maryland",
  "series": "Tracking Cartels Infographic Series",
  "asOf": "2020-06",
  "seriesUrl": "https://www.start.umd.edu/tracking-cartels-infographic-series",
  "briefs": [
    {
      "id": "operational_zones",
      "title": "Major Cartel Operational Zones in Mexico",
      "url": "https://www.start.umd.edu/pubs/JointCOEProject_TrackingCartels01_OperationalZonesMexico_ResearchBrief_June2020.pdf",
      "keyPoints": [
        "Major cartel fragmentation has led to increasingly adaptable, agile, and competitively violent criminal organizations.",
        "The geographical expansion of cartels has led to greater territorial contestation over drug plazas, trafficking routes, and illicit markets.",
        "Seeking greater profit, cartels are diversifying and increasing in criminal density through extortion, kidnapping, and money laundering.",
        "An estimated 90 percent of illicit drugs entering the United States pass through Mexico and the Central American isthmus."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cjng",
      "title": "The Violent Rise of Cártel de Jalisco Nueva Generación (CJNG)",
      "url": "https://www.start.umd.edu/pubs/JointCOEProject_TrackingCartels02_CJNG_ResearchBrief_June2020.pdf",
      "keyPoints": [
        "CJNG is one of the youngest cartels in Mexico yet considered one of, if not the, most powerful and violent.",
        "CJNG's assets are thought to be worth over $20 billion.",
        "Operationally present in 23 of Mexico's 32 states (with allies in all 32); led by founder Nemesio Oseguera Cervantes, 'El Mencho'.",
        "Captured the key ports of Veracruz, Manzanillo, and Lázaro Cárdenas; battles the Sinaloa Federation for Ciudad Juárez and Tijuana."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "avocado",
      "title": "The Pits: Violence in Michoacán Over Control of Avocado Trade",
      "url": "https://www.start.umd.edu/pubs/JointCOEProject_TrackingCartels03_AvocadoTrade_ResearchBrief_June2020.pdf",
      "keyPoints": [
        "Michoacán produces more than 1.5 million metric tons of avocados yearly (80 percent of Mexican production); Uruapan is the heart of the trade.",
        "CJNG competes violently with Nueva Familia Michoacana, the Tepalcatepec Cartel, and the Zicuirán Cartel to dominate this criminal economy.",
        "Extortion ('derecho de piso') of producers is charged monthly, often by hectares cultivated or kilograms exported; extortion is the highest reported crime in 14 of 32 states.",
        "August 2019: CJNG massacred 19 members of Los Viagras in Uruapan as the war over avocado territory expanded."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "huachicol",
      "title": "Huachicoleros: Violence in Guanajuato Over Control of Illicit Petroleum",
      "url": "https://www.start.umd.edu/pubs/JointCOEProject_TrackingCartels04_GuanajuatoIllicitPetroleum_June2020.pdf",
      "keyPoints": [
        "At least 22 of 32 states deal with fuel theft; highest concentration in Hidalgo, Puebla, Querétaro, Jalisco, Veracruz, México, Tamaulipas, and Guanajuato.",
        "CJNG and Cártel Santa Rosa de Lima (CSRL, a CJNG splinter) battle for the second 'Triángulo Rojo' of huachicol: Salamanca, Irapuato, and Celaya.",
        "Financial losses from fuel theft amount to around $1.1 billion annually; more than 15,000 illegal taps were identified in 2018.",
        "PEMEX operates over 14,000 km of pipelines; the Guanajuato triangle hosts a major refinery and multiple storage/distribution terminals."
      ]
    }
  ],
